   Use of these marks requires explicit written permission from:
   legal@nakhara.io
   
   This restriction does NOT apply to:
   - Factual references in documentation
   - Academic or research purposes
   - Fair use commentary

2. MAINNET LAUNCH RESTRICTION
   This software may be used to operate:
   ✅ Development networks (chain ID 1337, 31337, etc.)
   ✅ Private testing networks
   ✅ Academic research networks
   ✅ Contributing to the official Nakhara project
   
   ❌ PROHIBITED without explicit authorization:
   - Launching public mainnets with economic tokens claiming to be "Nakhara"
   - Operating networks that could confuse users with the official Nakhara Network
   - Creating token systems branded as "NAK" or "Nakhara Token"
   
   Authorization requests: mainnet-auth@nakhara.io

3. CHAIN IDENTITY REQUIREMENT
   Any modified version or fork MUST:
   - Use a different chain ID than official Nakhara networks
   - Use a different genesis hash
   - Clearly identify itself as a derivative work
   - NOT misrepresent itself as the official Nakhara Network
   
   Official chain IDs:
   - Testnet: 86137 (NAK testnet)
   - Mainnet: 86150 (reserved, not yet launched)

4. NETWORK COMPATIBILITY
   Forks and derivatives must implement clear differentiation:
   - Different network name in all user-facing interfaces
   - Different token symbol if implementing a token
   - Warning to users that it is NOT the official Nakhara Network
   
5. ENFORCEMENT
   Violation of these additional terms may result in:
   - Revocation of authorization to use this software
   - Legal action for trademark infringement
   - DMCA takedown requests
   - Community warnings and blacklisting
   
   Report violations: security@nakhara.io

6. OFFICIAL NETWORK REGISTRY
   Verify authentic Nakhara networks at:
   https://nakhara.io/networks
   
   Any network not listed there is NOT officially endorsed.

